<!--
    OUTER (cover) display, motorola arcfox (Razr 50 Ultra / Razr+ 2024).

    local:4630947043778501764  port 132  1080x1272  density 360
    "Built-in Screen", type INTERNAL on Android 16.

    Worth noting: on Android 14 stock reported this panel as
    name="HDMI Screen", type=EXTERNAL — a workaround for a framework without
    real flip support. Android 16 classifies it as a genuine internal secondary
    display. If this file is ever back-ported to a 22.x build, expect the
    EXTERNAL classification to matter.

    Flags observed in both versions: FLAG_PRESENTATION, FLAG_OWN_CONTENT_ONLY,
    FLAG_OWN_DISPLAY_GROUP, FLAG_ALLOWED_TO_BE_DEFAULT_DISPLAY. It sits in
    displayGroupId 1, layerStack 1. No cutout.

    The canSetBrightnessViaHwc quirk is carried over from zeekr, which needed it
    on its cover panel. UNVERIFIED on arcfox: if cover-display brightness
    control misbehaves, this line is the first thing to try removing.
-->
<displayConfiguration>
    <name>Outer Display</name>

    <quirks>
        <quirk>canSetBrightnessViaHwc</quirk>
    </quirks>

    <autoBrightness enabled="true">
    </autoBrightness>

    <densityMapping>
        <density>
            <width>1080</width>
            <height>1272</height>
            <density>360</density>
        </density>
    </densityMapping>
</displayConfiguration>
